AB  - Sustaining online volunteer engagement is essential for organizational success, particularly in resource-constrained environments. This article presents a comprehensive framework for motivating and retaining volunteers, integrating motivational theories, practical approaches, and future-oriented innovations. Core strategies include structured onboarding, recognition and feedback mechanisms, skill development, community-building, and technology integration. Challenges such as digital access, communication barriers, and volunteer isolation are addressed with adaptable solutions. Case studies illustrate effective interventions across diverse regions, while future trends—AI, automation, VR, and AR—are highlighted for their potential to transform volunteer management. By combining theory with practice, the article provides actionable guidance for cultivating engaged, skilled, and resilient online volunteer communities.
