DO  - 10.64357/neya-gjnps-gv-dt.009
AB  - This article explores strategies for sustaining volunteer engagement and retention in global networks. It identifies the drivers of motivation, including meaningful roles, communication, professional development, recognition, and flexible scheduling. The analysis emphasizes proactive support systems such as mentorship, wellness initiatives, and feedback loops, which prevent disengagement and enhance volunteer loyalty. Drawing on case studies from Crisis Text Line, Translators Without Borders, UN Volunteers, and other organizations, the article demonstrates that inclusive and adaptive engagement strategies are critical to long-term sustainability. It concludes that investing in recognition, professional growth, and responsive support builds resilient volunteer communities capable of delivering enduring social impact.
