TY  - JOUR
AU  - Elena Ancuța Zăvoianu
AU  - Simona Gabriela Ciucă
TI  - Volunteering as a Formative Experience in Adolescence: An Integrative Conceptual Model
JO  - Revista Romaneasca pentru Educatie Multidimensionala
PY  - 2026
DO  - 10.66388/rrem/18.1/05
AB  - This article proposes an integrative conceptual model that explains how volunteering functions as a formative experience during adolescence. Drawing on four theoretical traditions, the model traces causal pathways from experience characteristics through mediating processes to developmental outcomes. Self-Determination Theory accounts for the motivational dynamics underlying sustained engagement. The Positive Youth Development framework identifies the competencies that prosocial participation cultivates. Social Identity Theory addresses identity formation and the accumulation of social capital in group settings. Activity Theory grounds the analysis in the role of meaningful engagement for wellbeing. These perspectives are synthesised into a single framework specifying input variables, mediating mechanisms, developmental outcomes, moderating conditions, and risk factors. A central argument is that developmental gains depend on the quality of experience rather than participation alone. Key factors include alignment between the adolescent’s interests and the volunteer role, adequate organisational support, and safeguards against psychological strain. Sixteen testable propositions are derived, laying the groundwork for a systematic programme of longitudinal and cross-cultural research.
ER  - 

