AU  - Rachaphol Siriratpiriya
TI  - The Buddha Dharma Doctrine for Volunteer Rescuer within Pragmatic Work of Rescue and Public Relief Disaster
PY  - 2018
AB  - Lending a hand to dead body is a beginning point of rescuer and public relief disaster lead to Emergency Medical System in Thailand.  The motivation to become a volunteer rescuer has caused by oneself, families and communities besides, believed in good intentions and in matters of karma.  In addition pragmatic work has to be under Public Disaster Prevention and Mitigation Act, B.E. 2550 and Emergency Medical Act B.E. 2551. The Buddha Dharma Doctrine involved in volunteer rescuer of Rescue and Public Relief Disaster for the Dharma Theravada consists of Brahmavihara 4, Iddhipada 4, Gharavasa Dhamma 4, Sangahavatthu 4, Saraniyadhamma 6, and Anusati 10.  While the Mahayana faith in Bodhisattva lead the volunteer by qualification of Bodhisattva, Perfection 10, Ethic 10, and the great commitment.
